        ":question/id": "a5c334a0-b9d7-58f1-b30e-102327fa70dc",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "After charging the battery of a PC, the percentage of charge decreases at a rate of $c(t)=100\\cdot {5}^{-0.4t}$ percent per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the battery had completed its charge. What will be the rate of decrease after $10$ hours?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the amount of charge after $10$ hours, we have $t=10.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease of the amount of charge after $10$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(10) & =100\\cdot {5}^{-0.4(10)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {5}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{625} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $\\frac{4}{25}$ percent per hour.",
