      "question": {
        ":question/id": "43cee7e4-6ff9-5eeb-9102-bb7cf335c204",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t) = 4 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t) = 1 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000$.\n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2004$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change of the crocodile population is the birth rate minus the death rate.\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nSince $2004$ is $4$ years after $2000$, substitute $t=4$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(4)-D(4) & =4\\cdot e^{0.25(4)}-1\\cdot e^{0.25(4)} \\\\  & =3\\cdot e^{1} \\\\  & \\approx 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $8$ crocodiles per year.",
